From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:49:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Smoke test the x86_64 HAP on the OpenHarmony emulator

The OpenHarmony build produced an x86_64 HAP that nothing ran. The new
OpenHarmony emulator job boots the OpenHarmony 7.0 emulator of cargo-ohos
(QEMU with KVM, with the image that cargo-ohos 0.3.4 pins) on a
GitHub-hosted runner, installs the HAP and opens a page that
etc/ci/ohos_emulator_smoke_test.py serves to the guest. The page reports
back to the script after its load event and two animation frames. The
script then requires a screenshot to show the page's background over at
least a quarter of the screen, and fails on a panic in the log or an app
that is no longer running. The job uploads the screenshot, the device log
and the emulator logs.

The emulator accepts the unsigned HAP that the build produces without
signing material. The ArkWeb on-device suite does not run there: it needs
OpenHarmony's webview libraries with the SERVO branch, which the emulator
image does not have.

The script and the workflow only affect the OpenHarmony jobs, so pr_jobs
counts them as OHOS code.

Validation: on the x86_64 phone emulator of cargo-ohos 0.3.4 (KVM, booted in 18 s), `python3 etc/ci/ohos_emulator_smoke_test.py <x86_64 servoshell HAP of ohos-main f970c07d16f> --target <hdc connect-key>` passes in 6 s after a fresh boot: the page reports a 120 px wide heading and 67% of the screenshot shows its background. A screenshot of the home screen scores 0.7%, below the 25% threshold. In CI, the "OpenHarmony emulator" job uploads the screenshot as the ohos-emulator-smoke-test artifact.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; wrote the smoke test and the workflow, and ran the test on a local emulator)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
